WEBVTT

00:04.462 --> 00:06.923
[intriguing music playing]

00:11.011 --> 00:12.387
ZAGAN 50KM BERITH 10KM

00:12.470 --> 00:13.430
[tires screeching]

00:13.513 --> 00:14.931
- What the hell is that?
- [gasps]

00:19.769 --> 00:21.146
[uneasy music playing]

00:30.280 --> 00:32.157
[Fujita] Mr. En is dead.

00:32.907 --> 00:37.162
All the mushrooms created by his Magic
have begun to rot away.

00:37.245 --> 00:41.624
And because of that,
now the entire world knows he's gone.

00:43.543 --> 00:45.378
[frantic electronic music playing]

00:57.932 --> 00:59.517
[lyrics in Japanese]

02:10.922 --> 02:12.006
THE BEGINNING

02:12.090 --> 02:12.924
[music fades]

02:14.759 --> 02:16.594
[gradually intensifying warbling]

02:20.765 --> 02:21.683
[gasps]

02:21.766 --> 02:23.393
CHAOS SHOCK

02:23.476 --> 02:27.772
[Fujita] After I lost consciousness,
the mansion was plunged into chaos.

02:28.273 --> 02:31.526
Shin and Noi noticed something was wrong
and came back,

02:31.609 --> 02:33.194
but it was already too late.

02:33.987 --> 02:37.532
Whoever the murderer was,
he escaped through the air duct.

02:38.032 --> 02:40.201
He took Mr. En's head with him.

02:40.785 --> 02:42.704
Shin followed the trail of blood,

02:43.288 --> 02:47.584
but the culprit's tracks ended abruptly
inside the mansion.

02:49.043 --> 02:50.879
[goons sobbing]

02:53.298 --> 02:57.302
[Fujita] In the end,
the murderer got away without a trace.

03:02.348 --> 03:04.184
- [gasps]
- [Ebisu snickering]

03:04.267 --> 03:07.562
Ebisu tried looking for Kikurage
with treats in hand.

03:08.062 --> 03:11.608
[Fujita] That's right.
Kikurage has also disappeared.

03:12.442 --> 03:14.110
Chota has too.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.446
Even Nikaido has vanished.

03:17.989 --> 03:20.366
Ebisu was laughing as always,

03:20.450 --> 03:23.578
but for some reason,
she looked very lonely.

03:25.121 --> 03:29.000
Shin and the others asked me several times
about the headless man

03:29.083 --> 03:32.378
and the culprit
who ran off with Mr. En's head,

03:33.588 --> 03:36.007
but no matter how hard
I tried to remember,

03:37.467 --> 03:39.385
the blackness of that duct

03:40.345 --> 03:41.971
was too terrifying.

03:42.513 --> 03:44.599
I don't want to remember!

03:46.601 --> 03:51.022
It felt like somehow,
everything fell apart in an instant.

03:51.105 --> 03:52.523
[footsteps fading]

03:54.525 --> 03:57.528
[reporter] The effects of Mr. En's death
have been felt in every region.

03:57.612 --> 03:58.821
CHAOS SPREADS EVERYWHERE

03:58.905 --> 04:01.699
The Magic World,
which he ruled with his immense power,

04:01.783 --> 04:03.117
has lost its leader.

04:03.201 --> 04:04.827
The chaos is expected to spread...

04:04.911 --> 04:06.621
- [knocking on door]
- Hmm?

04:06.704 --> 04:08.623
Is that you, Noi? Come on in.

04:08.706 --> 04:11.209
Hey. You got a moment to talk?

04:12.710 --> 04:14.921
SCOOP: MR. EN'S MURDER
UNMASKING THE KILLER

04:15.004 --> 04:16.339
Look, Shin,

04:16.839 --> 04:19.425
to tell you the truth, I hated En.

04:19.509 --> 04:24.514
He used my Magic for his own convenience
ever since I was just a little kid,

04:24.597 --> 04:26.933
and he was always so arrogant about it.

04:27.016 --> 04:30.770
So no, I'm not sad
that mushroom freak is dead.

04:31.521 --> 04:33.731
However, without him around,

04:33.815 --> 04:36.442
the mansion is getting
completely out of control.

04:36.526 --> 04:40.947
Nobody here is cooking.
Nobody is cleaning. Nobody is working!

04:41.614 --> 04:44.409
Now who's supposed to take
the Cross-Eyes down?

04:44.492 --> 04:47.453
Guess everyone got scared and ran away.

04:47.954 --> 04:50.331
You don't have to love the guy, Noi,

04:50.415 --> 04:53.876
but it's thanks to Mr. En
that this world was somewhat decent.

04:54.544 --> 04:58.172
Hey, Shin, do you think
it was the Cross-Eyes' boss who killed En?

04:58.673 --> 05:00.174
Yeah it probably was.

05:00.258 --> 05:03.553
Fujita said he felt
the same physical discomfort.

05:04.095 --> 05:08.349
Most likely, it's the same guy
who fought En six years ago.

05:08.433 --> 05:12.145
Fine! Then let's hunt him down
and get En's head back.

05:12.228 --> 05:13.521
We can revive him!

05:13.604 --> 05:17.191
We could... if we had Kikurage,
but she's still missing.

05:17.734 --> 05:19.569
Yeah, but still,

05:19.652 --> 05:23.948
Kikurage, Chota and Nikaido,
all three of them might still be alive.

05:25.491 --> 05:26.326
Huh?

05:26.409 --> 05:29.620
Come on, Shin.
Are you just gonna sit there, or what?

05:30.413 --> 05:32.707
[Shin] Me? I'm a cleaner.

05:32.790 --> 05:35.293
I'm going to do the job I was hired to do.

05:35.376 --> 05:37.837
I'm gonna find this guy and kill him.

05:38.421 --> 05:40.381
I'm getting excited already.

05:41.674 --> 05:45.803
[giggles] Shin, you're a genius!
That's already in our job description!

05:45.887 --> 05:47.430
[squeals excitedly] I forgot.

05:47.513 --> 05:49.057
[gasps, relieved chuckling]

05:49.140 --> 05:53.311
I got so tired thinking about
all the little details! [chuckling]

05:53.394 --> 05:55.813
- I think I'll take a quick nap.
- Go back to your own room.

05:55.897 --> 05:56.939
Excuse me.

05:57.023 --> 05:58.649
- [gasps]
- Am I interrupting?

05:58.733 --> 06:00.860
- [Shin] It's not what it looks like!
- Hello.

06:00.943 --> 06:04.947
- [Shin] Oh, Turkey.
- [Turkey] It's been a while.

06:08.242 --> 06:09.327
[Asu] Nikaido.

06:10.536 --> 06:11.746
Nikaido.

06:12.997 --> 06:14.123
Nikaido!

06:14.916 --> 06:17.710
Kawajiri... Big bro.

06:24.384 --> 06:26.135
[gasps] Caiman.

06:26.719 --> 06:28.638
Hey, Caiman.

06:28.721 --> 06:31.891
I'm Aikawa. You've got the wrong guy.

06:31.974 --> 06:32.892
[gasps]

06:32.975 --> 06:36.396
- I'm a Sorcerer, just like you.
- [Nikaido gasps]

06:37.230 --> 06:39.357
You're wrong. I gave it up!

06:39.982 --> 06:41.567
I gave up Magic!

06:42.193 --> 06:44.028
It's because of my power.

06:44.112 --> 06:46.114
I'm sorry, Yakumo! [gasps]

06:46.197 --> 06:48.116
[tense music playing]

06:52.954 --> 06:54.122
- [bubbling]
- [panting]

06:54.205 --> 06:57.125
[Yakumo] Nikaido,
I've always been a very lucky girl.

06:57.708 --> 06:59.377
Do you know why?

07:00.962 --> 07:03.131
[Nikaido whimpering, panting]

07:03.214 --> 07:05.633
Yakumo!

07:05.716 --> 07:06.676
[music fades]

07:07.343 --> 07:09.137
[gasps, sobbing]

07:09.720 --> 07:10.805
It's all my fault.

07:11.305 --> 07:13.433
If I hadn't used Magic... [sobs]

07:13.516 --> 07:14.600
[creaking]

07:14.684 --> 07:16.644
BLACK BOX

07:18.771 --> 07:20.481
Where am I?

07:20.982 --> 07:24.277
Did I come here
because of this square thing?

07:24.360 --> 07:26.904
I don't even know which button does what.

07:27.572 --> 07:28.906
What a piece of junk!

07:28.990 --> 07:30.450
Tell me where I am!

07:30.950 --> 07:31.868
Huh?

07:32.743 --> 07:34.287
I know this river...

07:35.705 --> 07:36.622
[Nikaido gasps]

07:36.706 --> 07:38.416
It's my grandparents!

07:38.499 --> 07:40.376
Grandma! Grandpa!

07:40.960 --> 07:42.670
Who are you calling "Grandma"?

07:42.753 --> 07:45.131
- I'm not that old.
- [grandpa] Whose kid is this?

07:45.214 --> 07:47.884
Huh? Oh, but, Grandpa, I'm Nikaido!

07:47.967 --> 07:49.343
[grandpa] I don't know you.

07:49.427 --> 07:52.638
Sorry little girl. We just happened
to be taking a walk around here.

07:53.514 --> 07:57.226
[Nikaido] Grandpa and Grandma
are acting different than usual.

07:57.727 --> 08:01.230
Could this be sometime in the past?

08:02.231 --> 08:05.151
In that case,
is this what my Magic can do?

08:06.986 --> 08:08.654
[uneasy music playing]

08:10.364 --> 08:12.450
[Nikaido] You won't believe it, big bro.

08:12.533 --> 08:15.786
Today, I went into the past
by using that weird box.

08:15.870 --> 08:19.373
I even met Grandpa and Grandma there
when they were young.

08:19.457 --> 08:20.917
- [grandma] Hmm?
- [grandpa] Hmm?

08:21.000 --> 08:22.960
[all laughing]

08:23.044 --> 08:26.088
Oh, Nikaido,
time manipulation magic is just a myth.

08:26.172 --> 08:27.381
It doesn't exist.

08:27.465 --> 08:29.383
[grandpa] Don't lie, Nikaido.

08:29.467 --> 08:30.676
[Nikaido] I'm not lying!

08:31.886 --> 08:32.929
Oh, wait.

08:33.721 --> 08:34.680
Where's Yakumo?

08:35.640 --> 08:36.891
Yakumo?

08:37.517 --> 08:39.185
[grandpa] What do you mean by "Yakumo"?

08:41.812 --> 08:42.688
[Nikaido] Huh?

08:44.774 --> 08:46.108
[water lapping]

08:46.609 --> 08:50.196
[Nikaido] Why is everyone pretending
they don't know Yakumo?

08:50.279 --> 08:53.616
It's like she never existed at all.

08:54.283 --> 08:57.995
[Yakumo] When I was a baby,
I floated down this river.

08:58.079 --> 09:01.707
Our grandparents just happened
to be passing by and picked me up.

09:01.791 --> 09:02.708
Oh...

09:02.792 --> 09:05.294
[Yakumo] If they had looked away
for even a second,

09:05.378 --> 09:07.713
I would've probably stayed in the water!

09:07.797 --> 09:09.966
- [gasping]
- [uneasy music playing]

09:10.049 --> 09:12.718
- [Nikaido sobbing]
- [mournful music playing]

09:14.303 --> 09:15.471
[Nikaido gasps]

09:15.555 --> 09:17.974
[whimpering, panting]

09:21.811 --> 09:24.480
Yakumo!

09:24.564 --> 09:25.481
[gasps]

09:27.692 --> 09:29.443
[dramatic music playing]

09:30.194 --> 09:31.612
AN UNNAMED SOUL LIES HERE

09:31.696 --> 09:33.614
- [Asu] Nikaido!
- [Nikaido gasps]

09:34.115 --> 09:36.617
Kawajiri. Big bro...

09:38.619 --> 09:42.707
[Asu] This is a town about
200 kilometers south of En's mansion.

09:43.207 --> 09:45.668
While I was waiting for you to wake,

09:45.751 --> 09:49.130
I purchased some healing smoke
and healed both of our wounds.

09:49.213 --> 09:50.923
Wow, thanks, Asu.

09:51.424 --> 09:53.884
My arms and legs are all back to normal.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.720
Hang on. Wait.

09:55.803 --> 09:58.723
But why did the healing smoke
start working now?

09:58.806 --> 10:00.891
I thought the mushrooms in my body...

10:02.018 --> 10:03.311
He was killed?

10:03.811 --> 10:07.148
No way! How is it possible that En...?

10:07.231 --> 10:09.108
Do you think it was Caiman?

10:09.191 --> 10:11.777
Who knows? Your guess is as good as mine.

10:11.861 --> 10:14.905
But word on the street is
that the Cross-Eyes killed him.

10:15.781 --> 10:16.907
The Cross-Eyes?

10:16.991 --> 10:22.163
I don't know if it's Caiman or Aikawa,
but if you wanna find him, I'll help you.

10:22.246 --> 10:23.914
Okay, Asu. Thanks.

10:23.998 --> 10:27.293
That reminds me, you talk in your sleep.

10:27.376 --> 10:30.171
In the middle of a nightmare,
you called me Kawajiri.

10:30.254 --> 10:33.591
I don't think I ever told you my name.

10:34.759 --> 10:38.387
And you said
I saved your life a long time ago.

10:38.471 --> 10:41.599
I wonder if this has
something to do with your Magic?

10:42.391 --> 10:46.103
Do you happen to remember
way back when we first met?

10:48.397 --> 10:52.193
I was just about to enter
the final stage of the Devil Exam.

10:53.402 --> 10:55.946
The last few days of the exam
are purposely set

10:56.030 --> 10:58.115
to coincide with the Blue Night.

10:58.199 --> 10:59.617
- [gasps]
- [grunts]

10:59.700 --> 11:00.743
[gasps]

11:02.036 --> 11:06.082
[Asu] All sorts of people were hunting me
in order to become my partner.

11:07.458 --> 11:10.586
I couldn't use Magic
until the exam was over.

11:10.670 --> 11:13.339
So, as you can imagine, I was on edge.

11:14.131 --> 11:15.466
And that was the day

11:15.549 --> 11:17.468
when the two of us first met.

11:20.513 --> 11:23.974
For some reason,
you wouldn't leave my side.

11:24.975 --> 11:26.352
And later that day...

11:26.435 --> 11:27.853
[struggling grunts]

11:27.937 --> 11:31.148
What now?
You gonna use Magic to save yourself?

11:31.232 --> 11:34.235
Or give up on the Devil Exam
and make us your partners?

11:34.318 --> 11:37.488
[strains] Like I'd ever make a contract
with you guys.

11:37.571 --> 11:39.490
- Huh?
- [Nikaido yelling]

11:39.573 --> 11:40.574
[pained grunt]

11:42.702 --> 11:44.537
- [Nikaido grunts, yells]
- Huh? Oof!

11:44.620 --> 11:46.914
- What?
- Go, get out of here!

11:46.997 --> 11:48.874
[thug 2] Not so fast! [grunts]

11:50.000 --> 11:54.672
Thanks to you saving me,
I was able to go on and become a Devil.

11:56.632 --> 11:58.926
I went to thank you
after I became a Devil,

11:59.969 --> 12:03.431
but you had already started thinking
about living in the Hole.

12:04.640 --> 12:06.934
By using my Devil powers,

12:07.017 --> 12:10.563
I learned that your Magic had
something to do with time.

12:10.646 --> 12:13.983
I know you've always refused
to use your abilities,

12:14.483 --> 12:17.278
Long ago they took
something very precious to you.

12:18.195 --> 12:21.449
But you aren't
that scared little child anymore.

12:22.032 --> 12:24.285
Use your Magic, Nikaido.

12:24.368 --> 12:27.830
Use your Magic
and take back what was taken from you.

12:28.497 --> 12:31.542
No, I can't... I can't do that, Asu.

12:31.625 --> 12:33.836
My Magic is more dangerous than you know.

12:35.004 --> 12:38.883
Besides, I'm the reason
you were turned back into a Sorcerer.

12:39.675 --> 12:43.846
[chuckles softly] You're the reason
I could become a Devil in the first place.

12:43.929 --> 12:47.850
I don't mind it.
I'd give up being a Devil for you any day.

12:48.434 --> 12:49.435
Asu...

12:53.397 --> 12:56.025
I'm going to take back what I lost.

12:57.777 --> 12:59.737
[Kasukabe] Ever since that En guy died,

12:59.820 --> 13:02.281
mansion security has been
pretty understaffed,

13:02.364 --> 13:03.449
hasn't it, Johnson?

13:03.532 --> 13:04.575
[Jonson chitters]

13:04.658 --> 13:07.661
We still haven't found the room
where they summon Devils.

13:07.745 --> 13:09.830
- [Jonson growling]
- [gasps] What wrong, Jonson?

13:09.914 --> 13:11.165
- [Jonson yells]
- Huh?

13:11.665 --> 13:13.709
Good evening, Doctor.

13:13.793 --> 13:17.463
Oh, Haru? You turned back into a Sorcerer?

13:17.546 --> 13:19.298
[Haru laughing evilly]

13:22.468 --> 13:23.719
[growls]

13:24.428 --> 13:27.723
[both] Pretty surprising.
It was a huge success.

13:27.807 --> 13:29.141
[Kasukabe and Jonson gasp]

13:29.225 --> 13:30.726
[Kasukabe] What are you talking about?

13:30.810 --> 13:33.479
I wanted it to be
a surprise for you, Hayes.

13:33.562 --> 13:36.232
[Devil] Both of us are the real me.

13:36.315 --> 13:41.362
[Haru] Although, it is dangerous.
If I stay out for too long, I'll die.

13:42.071 --> 13:43.614
[both] That's no bueno.

13:43.697 --> 13:46.700
I feel more at ease in this form anyway.

13:46.784 --> 13:48.744
[Kasukabe] Devils are amazing.

13:48.828 --> 13:51.622
[Haru and Devil] Obviously.
We're invincible.

13:51.705 --> 13:53.833
I'd love to dissect you some time.

13:53.916 --> 13:59.129
[Devil and Haru laugh] Oh, Doctor,
you always did have the silliest ideas.

13:59.213 --> 14:01.048
[dramatic music playing]

14:01.131 --> 14:02.633
[Devil chuckling]

14:03.425 --> 14:05.719
To celebrate our reunion properly,

14:05.803 --> 14:08.389
why don't I sing you
one of my original songs?

14:08.472 --> 14:09.390
Huh?

14:09.473 --> 14:10.349
HUMANS
BY HARU

14:10.432 --> 14:12.893
♪ Tiny, inferior creatures
That's what humans are ♪

14:12.977 --> 14:15.396
♪ I eat them when I'm hungry
But they're not tasty ♪

14:15.479 --> 14:16.397
♪ So lame when scared ♪

14:16.480 --> 14:20.401
♪ They live 90 years at most
Ah, too funny ♪

14:20.484 --> 14:21.527
[music stops#]

14:22.486 --> 14:24.196
[chuckling]

14:24.280 --> 14:26.699
That's just a little number about humans.

14:26.782 --> 14:30.119
I'm really into singing
about my true feelings lately.

14:30.202 --> 14:31.912
[Kasukabe] Uh, anyway,

14:31.996 --> 14:35.332
I was looking for you.
I wanted to ask for your help.

14:35.416 --> 14:37.543
Will you come back with me to the mansion?

14:37.626 --> 14:39.962
[Devil and Haru] Don't be in such a hurry.

14:40.045 --> 14:43.841
There's still plenty of time
for you to see my special trick.

14:44.383 --> 14:47.094
You know, you've changed a bit.

14:47.177 --> 14:49.680
[Turkey blowing]

14:50.848 --> 14:52.725
I figured this time around,

14:52.808 --> 14:56.687
we should make the doll
using the fastest baking method available.

14:57.730 --> 15:02.192
Although, I never thought I'd be asked
to make a doll of Mr. En like this...

15:02.943 --> 15:06.697
I hope this will eventually help us
catch the person who killed him.

15:06.780 --> 15:08.991
You can leave that part to us.

15:09.074 --> 15:12.202
Make us the best doll you got, Turkey.
- [Ebisu giggling]

15:12.286 --> 15:14.204
[jaunty music playing]

15:14.288 --> 15:15.289
[Turkey] To begin,

15:15.372 --> 15:19.209
cut the cheese, vegetables,
and salami to the ideal thickness.

15:19.293 --> 15:20.169
[Ebisu laughing]

15:20.252 --> 15:23.339
[Turkey] Choose a dough
that has been fermented to perfection,

15:24.214 --> 15:27.593
lightly flour it,
and roll it into a circle.

15:29.178 --> 15:33.599
Next, stretch it out and make it even.

15:34.266 --> 15:38.145
Cover the dough
with a generous spread of tomato sauce,

15:38.646 --> 15:41.357
put the toppings on,
and sprinkle powdered cheese.

15:41.941 --> 15:46.153
Finally, take the smoke
that most embodies Mr. En,

15:46.236 --> 15:48.113
infuse it into this oil can,

15:48.197 --> 15:49.865
and pour it over the dough.

15:52.451 --> 15:53.869
That all goes in the oven.

15:53.953 --> 15:55.663
[flames crackling]

15:56.956 --> 15:59.959
[Turkey] All that's left
is to wait for it to bake.

16:01.043 --> 16:02.795
You know, I've been thinking.

16:02.878 --> 16:04.088
If we follow this doll,

16:04.171 --> 16:06.715
it's likely we're gonna have to
fight the Cross-Eyes again.

16:06.799 --> 16:08.801
Ugh, what's taking them so long?

16:08.884 --> 16:11.136
Sounds like you don't remember
the way they worked us over

16:11.220 --> 16:13.472
back in the Hydra Forest, then, Noi.

16:13.555 --> 16:15.224
Of course I remember.

16:15.307 --> 16:18.644
They attacked the part
that stops you from producing smoke.

16:18.727 --> 16:20.854
That's exactly my point,

16:21.355 --> 16:24.900
but this time,
Kasukabe pinpointed the smoke's location

16:24.984 --> 16:27.820
to work out the places
they're likely to target

16:27.903 --> 16:29.780
[Noi] Why, that little nerd...

16:29.863 --> 16:33.033
- [Turkey] It should be done baking soon.
- [Ebisu giggling]

16:33.117 --> 16:34.243
[oven dings]

16:34.326 --> 16:35.786
[sizzling]

16:35.869 --> 16:39.790
- Let's cut him out from the dough.
- [giggling] Pizza butt!

16:39.873 --> 16:41.500
[laughing hysterically]

16:52.386 --> 16:53.595
The doll is finished.

16:53.679 --> 16:57.057
Soon it will begin
making its way back to the corpse.

16:57.641 --> 17:00.853
The lower part of Mr. En's body
is down in the morgue.

17:01.353 --> 17:03.439
Is there a chance that it could go there?

17:03.522 --> 17:05.190
[Turkey] No need to worry.

17:05.274 --> 17:08.736
The doll specifically reacts
to the tumor in the head.

17:08.819 --> 17:09.778
[goon 1 grunts]

17:10.529 --> 17:13.699
- [gasps] Whoa, he's already moving out!
- [Shin] Follow him!

17:13.782 --> 17:14.783
[Noi grunts]

17:14.867 --> 17:16.452
[Turkey] Oh, Mr. En,

17:16.535 --> 17:20.456
how nice it would be
to see the real you one more time...

17:20.539 --> 17:22.082
[suspenseful music playing]

17:22.166 --> 17:24.126
This thing really is a doll.

17:24.626 --> 17:28.839
Sure, it looks like En,
but you can really see the flaws up close.

17:28.922 --> 17:33.677
I'll say. He's Mr. En
but without his mushrooms or Kikurage.

17:34.178 --> 17:37.306
Didn't think it'd be so sad
to watch him wander around.

17:38.265 --> 17:41.185
- Huh? Oh, everyone's here!
- Uh, uh, Fujita!

17:43.270 --> 17:45.939
[whimpering] En? E...

17:46.023 --> 17:47.149
[Noi] Wait. It's a doll!

17:49.401 --> 17:51.320
[Ebisu laughing hysterically]

17:51.403 --> 17:53.072
Oh, brother...

17:53.739 --> 17:56.200
- Hey, Shin, the doll's gone!
- [Shin] What?!

17:56.283 --> 17:58.077
[Shin and Noi breathing heavily]

17:58.160 --> 17:59.787
[dramatic music playing]

18:03.916 --> 18:06.835
Wait, the doll of Mr. En
can use the Broom?

18:06.919 --> 18:07.961
- [Noi] Hey!
- Huh?

18:08.045 --> 18:09.838
Hurry, jump on!

18:09.922 --> 18:11.840
[dramatic music continues]

18:24.770 --> 18:26.438
[Shin] We'll lose sight of him
at this rate!

18:26.522 --> 18:29.483
[Noi] Why do we store that Broom
with so much smoke in the tank?

18:29.566 --> 18:33.320
You keep chasing him on this.
I'll get ahead of him from the roof.-

18:33.403 --> 18:34.571
[Noi] Got it!

18:35.072 --> 18:36.990
[Shin grunting]

18:39.076 --> 18:39.993
[yells]

18:44.832 --> 18:47.251
Damn it, he's so fast! [grunts]

18:49.920 --> 18:51.839
This should slow him down...

18:51.922 --> 18:53.841
Take that!

18:57.886 --> 19:00.264
That was good thinking, Noi.

19:00.806 --> 19:01.974
[grunts]

19:03.559 --> 19:04.560
[grunts]

19:05.894 --> 19:07.813
[steady beep, dwindling beep]

19:08.981 --> 19:11.316
[Noi chuckling] Yes!
All right, we got him!

19:11.400 --> 19:12.526
[Shin sighs]

19:12.609 --> 19:13.986
Oh brother.

19:14.069 --> 19:15.863
[dramatic music playing]

19:20.409 --> 19:23.579
I was very surprised
when I heard the news that En had died.

19:23.662 --> 19:27.332
Do you really think
it was actually the boss who killed him?

19:27.416 --> 19:30.836
Who else would run off with En's head?
It had to be the boss!

19:30.919 --> 19:32.171
We'll be fine.

19:32.254 --> 19:33.338
If something happens,

19:33.422 --> 19:35.966
we got plenty of healing smoke
right here with us.

19:36.049 --> 19:39.887
[Tetsujo] I was worried
when Dokuga killed the Shaitan guys,

19:40.554 --> 19:43.974
but now that En's dead,
we don't have to worry about being found.

19:44.057 --> 19:45.684
Is that great timing or what?

19:45.767 --> 19:47.978
I'm telling you,
the boss is coming back right now!

19:49.188 --> 19:53.192
Dokuga, are you sure
you know where to find him?

19:53.901 --> 19:54.985
I have an idea.

19:59.948 --> 20:00.991
[music fades]

20:06.705 --> 20:08.540
[phone ringing]

20:11.043 --> 20:12.753
[phone ringing]

20:15.631 --> 20:17.257
[phone ringing]

20:20.469 --> 20:22.888
- [flies buzzing]
- [phone ringing]

20:24.556 --> 20:26.225
[phone ringing]

20:29.061 --> 20:30.312
[phone ringing]

20:30.395 --> 20:31.480
INCOMING CALL

20:31.563 --> 20:33.482
- [outgoing call tone, phone picks up]
- [gasps]

20:37.486 --> 20:39.238
- [Dokuga] Boss?
- What?!

20:39.321 --> 20:42.407
I called over and over again.

20:42.991 --> 20:43.951
Where were you?

20:44.034 --> 20:45.244
Boss, is that you?

20:45.327 --> 20:47.663
It's me, Ushishimada, remember?

20:47.746 --> 20:50.123
So was it really you who killed En, Boss?

20:50.207 --> 20:52.084
[Saji] Is the boss there?
What's he saying?

20:52.167 --> 20:54.878
[all talking over each other]

20:54.962 --> 20:56.004
CALL ENDED

20:56.088 --> 20:58.507
- [all moaning]
- He hung up.

20:58.590 --> 21:01.510
[dial tone beeping]

21:02.636 --> 21:05.430
[Ushishimada] Was that really
the boss just now?

21:05.514 --> 21:06.974
What do you think Dokuga?

21:07.057 --> 21:07.891
[gasps]

21:07.975 --> 21:10.394
- Dokuga!
- Oh, dear.

21:11.645 --> 21:13.480
We should just get going.

21:13.563 --> 21:15.524
[tense music playing]

21:21.238 --> 21:25.242
[Shin] Is Mr. En's head really
somewhere in this run-down building?

21:25.325 --> 21:28.161
Don't forget,
probably the Cross-Eyes' boss too.

21:28.245 --> 21:33.417
I can finally give that bastard
some payback. [chuckling]

21:39.214 --> 21:40.340
All right!

21:41.967 --> 21:42.801
Hmm?

21:42.884 --> 21:45.304
What's the matter, Shin? Something wrong?

21:46.471 --> 21:49.891
It feels kinda like
there's been somebody watching me lately.

21:50.392 --> 21:53.979
- Huh?
- No, it's fine. Forget it.

21:57.441 --> 21:59.985
This is it.
I think it's that room up there.

22:02.946 --> 22:03.822
[all gasp]

22:04.406 --> 22:06.366
Is that... the boss?

22:06.950 --> 22:08.618
[tense music continues]

22:08.702 --> 22:09.870
[elevator dings]

22:11.079 --> 22:12.372
[music intensifies]

22:20.964 --> 22:22.924
- [music fades]
- [gasps] This room?

22:23.008 --> 22:25.385
Oh man, the boss is inside!

22:32.017 --> 22:34.394
[Dokuga] Someone's in there.
I'm sure of it.

22:34.478 --> 22:35.395
[all gasp]

22:35.479 --> 22:37.105
[Saji] What do we do?

22:37.189 --> 22:39.691
[Ushishimada] Uh...
let's try opening it, yeah?

22:39.775 --> 22:42.235
[Tetsujo] No, no,
we should ring the intercom.

22:42.319 --> 22:43.153
[all gasp]

22:44.696 --> 22:46.156
[chuckling gleefully]

22:46.239 --> 22:47.908
- [dramatic music playing]
- Well, well, well.

22:47.991 --> 22:50.160
Whoa! Look who's here!

22:50.243 --> 22:52.120
We found the bastards!

22:52.204 --> 22:54.664
[gasps] It's the En family cleaners!

22:55.916 --> 22:57.501
[Shin laughing menacingly]

22:59.586 --> 23:00.879
[music fades]

23:01.922 --> 23:03.382
[Japanese theme song playing]

24:29.634 --> 24:30.927
THE END

24:31.011 --> 24:33.096
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 20.

24:33.180 --> 24:35.765
Turns out a lot of things
were made with En's Magic.

24:35.849 --> 24:37.225
Haru loves to sing.

24:37.309 --> 24:39.186
Asu is loyal to Nikaido.

24:39.269 --> 24:43.523
What we're going to learn in Episode 21,
it's still... lost in chaos.

24:43.607 --> 24:45.942
This is Dorohedoro!
